jobs.description:
Mandarin Oriental Conservatorium is looking for a Chef de Partie to join our Ottolenghi team.Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional. Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world's most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences.

Functie-eisen:
As Chef de Partie, you will be responsible for the following duties:
• You will be supervising the day-to-day operation of a designated section within the kitchen, overseeing all aspects of food production;
• Delivering highest levels of quality and precision, preparing dishes in line with recipes and standards;
• Maintaining highest levels of hygiene and cost control;
• You will act as a role model and mentor to the junior members in the kitchen brigade, guiding and supporting them in their development.Yotam Ottolenghi's restaurants are renowned London eateries known for vibrant, Middle Eastern-inspired dishes, offering everything from delis to full restaurants, featuring seasonal ingredients, bold flavors, and colorful displays, perfect for breakfast, lunch, and dinner.As Chef de Partie we expect from you: 
• Recent/current experience in the same position to that of Chef de Partie for at least two years;
• A passionate and quality-driven approach to cooking;
• Teamwork, being able to work closely with 6-8 chefs on shift;
• Experience in inspired Middle Eastern cooking cuisine;
• Good knowledge of English language (written and spoken);
• Familiar with hygiene code and HACCP regulations;
• Ability to work evenings and weekend shif

Vacaturebeschrijving   
In Best, you can start as a Production Worker at a growing company that produces vegetarian meat products. You will learn the job on the work floor, work Monday to Friday on the day shift and earn a gross starting salary of € 15.94 per hour. Do you enjoy the job and does it work well for both sides? Then there is a possibility of getting a direct contract with our client in the future.
Over de functieAs a Production Worker, you will work together with your colleagues to produce vegetarian meat products. You will help ensure that the production process runs smoothly and that the products are ready for the shelves. Your responsibilities will include:
- Supporting the production process;
- Preparing and processing vegetarian meat products;
- Checking the quality of the products;
- Packaging and preparing products for shipment;
- Keeping your work area clean and tidy;
- Following all applicable hygiene and safety regulations.

You will work Monday to Friday from 7:00 AM to 4:00 PM. A great job where you will work with a friendly team, develop your skills and contribute to the food of the future!
Wat wij bieden- As a Production Worker, you will earn a gross hourly wage between € 15.05 and € 15.94;
- You will receive €0.23 per kilometre for travel expenses;
- 8% holiday allowance and 27 days of paid annual leave;
- Pension scheme from your first working day;
- Choose between weekly or every-four-weeks payment of your salary;
- Enjoy the weekly soup day every Tuesday;
- A job with the possibility of a direct contract with the company.

Wat wij vragen- You speak Dutch and/or English;
- You are available to work 40 hours per week;
- Working in a chilled environment of 8 to 12 degrees Celsius is not a problem for you.

